  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Skat. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Skat is widely regarded as Germany's national card game and one of the best 3-player trick-taking games ever devised. It features complex bidding based on 'Game Value', a unique trump hierarchy (Jacks are highest), and three main contract types (Suit, Grand, Null). The 'Soloist' plays against two defenders. The game combines luck, skill in hand evaluation, and precise card play.",
    objective: 'Soloist: Score 61+ points (in Suit/Grand) or lose no tricks (Null). Defenders: Prevent Soloist.',
    gameplay: "Soloist can pick up the Skat (Hand game multiplier if they don't). Discard 2 cards. Declare game.",
    keyRules: [
      'Deal 3-4-3; two cards (Skat) face-down to the table. Bidding (Reizen) determines declarer and minimum game value.',
      'Declarer may pick up the Skat and discard two cards, or play Hand without picking up. Declare game type: Suit, Grand, or Null.',
      'Jacks are the highest trumps (J-clubs, J-spades, J-hearts, J-diamonds). Must follow suit; may trump when void. Ten tricks; forehand leads first.',
      'Soloist needs 61+ card points (Suit/Grand) or lose every trick (Null). Card points: A=11, 10=10, K=4, Q=3, J=2; 9-7=0.',
    ],
